<title>PANAMA: Panama awards dam project to Mexico, Canada group.</title>
<headline>Panama awards dam project to Mexico, Canada group.</headline>
<dateline>PANAMA CITY 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Panama awarded the contract for the country's second largest hydro-electric power station to a consortium headed by Mexico's Empresas ICA Sociedad Controladora SA de CV and General Electric Co's General Electric Canada Inc, a government official said Monday.</p>
<p>The consortium presented the lowest bid of $199.1 million to design and build a $300 million, 132-megawatt dam in western Chiriqui province, 150 miles (240 km) from the capital, said a source with the Institute of Water Resources and Electricity (IHRE).</p>
<p>The design phase is set to begin in June and construction in November, he said.  The project should be finished by the year 2001, he said.</p>
<p>((-- Laurens Grant, Panama City newsroom, 507 2237739))</p>
